WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.099 --> 00:00:13.599
In 2017, it'll be 70 years since India broke
off from the British Empire and became an

00:00:13.599 --> 00:00:18.210
independent country, which today, is actually
the largest democracy in the world.

00:00:18.210 --> 00:00:23.449
In these 70 years, India has managed to implement
a political system, with more than 1,000 parties,

00:00:23.449 --> 00:00:32.460
and high female participation that is totally
unprecedented in such a poor country.

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:35.399
Of course, we should wait before we pop the
champagne...

00:00:35.399 --> 00:00:39.949
Because we can't precisely say that these
70 years of independence have gone brilliantly

00:00:39.949 --> 00:00:44.030
in this gigantic country of more than 1.2
billion people:

00:00:44.030 --> 00:00:50.489
poverty, inequality, a terrible caste system
and many, many problems with women's rights

00:00:50.489 --> 00:00:52.679
have continued to shake this nation.

00:00:52.679 --> 00:00:53.679
That...

00:00:53.679 --> 00:00:59.760
And 4 wars with Pakistan, which has become
something of an archenemy…

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:04.900
But, if you really want to know why we might
claim that India CAN'T be that proud of the

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:10.780
last 70 years, well, we only need to compare
this country's evolution with that of China.

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:15.090
See, when Deng Xiaoping launched his policy
to open China up to the world and change it's

00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:21.250
economic model back in the 1980s, the sizes
of these two economic giants, China and India,

00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:23.189
were similar.

00:01:23.189 --> 00:01:26.979
In 2016, however, China's GDP was 5 times
higher.

00:01:26.979 --> 00:01:35.049
Check out this graph:
And not only that, these differences repeat

00:01:35.049 --> 00:01:39.590
in practically every statistic - social and
economic.

00:01:39.590 --> 00:01:40.590
Another example?

00:01:40.590 --> 00:01:45.240
Well, while China's illiteracy affects less
than 4% of the population, in India almost

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:50.460
1 out of 3 people can't read or write.

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:56.520
So, considering all this, we could almost
reach the conclusion that the only good thing

00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:59.060
that this country has achieved has been its
democracy, right?

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:04.319
Well wait a second, because it seems that
this poverty and injustice situation is beginning

00:02:04.319 --> 00:02:09.759
to shift...

00:02:09.759 --> 00:02:15.140
More and more experts are betting that the
21st century will be, above all, India's century.

00:02:15.140 --> 00:02:19.080
That is to say, that in the next few decades
we'll witness how this country emerges from

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:22.630
the developing world to become an economic
super power.

00:02:22.630 --> 00:02:26.600
Many companies, such as Amazon and Apple are
already betting on this transformation and

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:29.570
are paying close attention to this huge market.

00:02:29.570 --> 00:02:34.570
They understand that, if expectations are
met, in the next few years we could see one

00:02:34.570 --> 00:02:38.260
of the biggest business opportunities in history.

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:41.890
And it's not just companies.

00:02:41.890 --> 00:02:46.440
The Delhi government's own expectations are
so high that they expect this country's transformation

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:51.350
to be at least as impressive as that of China
in the coming decades.

00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:54.250
For this reason, they want to be prepared.

00:02:54.250 --> 00:02:59.690
They are contemplating, for example, building
250 airports, 6 new macro-ports and creating

00:02:59.690 --> 00:03:05.670
more than 150 million new and accessible homes
in the next 10 years alone…

00:03:05.670 --> 00:03:08.670
In other words...

00:03:08.670 --> 00:03:11.650
everything indicates that we may see India's
great takeoff.

00:03:11.650 --> 00:03:13.930
Which is a good thing, right?

00:03:13.930 --> 00:03:27.790
Well keep one thing in mind, Beijing doesn't
like this, not at all…

00:03:27.790 --> 00:03:31.180
DISTRUST AND RESENTMENT

00:03:31.180 --> 00:03:33.450
China is India's main trading partner.

00:03:33.450 --> 00:03:37.790
However, despite this, Chinese authorities
look at India's growing economic, political

00:03:37.790 --> 00:03:40.900
and military capacity with a lot of distrust.

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:44.730
This is because this is a time when China
wants to gain political influence, and this

00:03:44.730 --> 00:03:47.240
change in India doesn't suit them at all...

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:51.870
India is perhaps the only country in Asia
with enough potential to offset China's political

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:53.150
power in the region.

00:03:53.150 --> 00:03:56.890
After all, we are talking about what will
soon be the most populated country on earth.

00:03:56.890 --> 00:04:01.870
And, there's even analysts who affirm that
this has already happened - that India has

00:04:01.870 --> 00:04:04.590
surpassed China in population size.

00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:05.980
But it isn't only that...

00:04:05.980 --> 00:04:09.680
Because of the one-child policy that affected
China for so many years, India's population

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:14.570
has - and will have – more young people
and less elderly people.

00:04:14.570 --> 00:04:17.070
Which is quite an advantage.

00:04:17.070 --> 00:04:28.510
Given these circumstances it's easy to understand
Beijing's distrust 

00:04:28.510 --> 00:04:29.570
of India.

00:04:29.570 --> 00:04:31.970
Don't you think?

00:04:31.970 --> 00:04:32.970
Now...

00:04:32.970 --> 00:04:37.720
Don't think that this feeling only exists
in political offices, not at all in fact.

00:04:37.720 --> 00:04:41.790
This growing rivalry is also reflected on
the streets.

00:04:41.790 --> 00:04:44.560
Consider the following data:

00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:50.190
According to a survey published in 2016 by
the Pew Research Center, only 1 in 4 Chinese

00:04:50.190 --> 00:04:52.880
people have a favorable opinion of India.

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:58.250
And in India's case, it isn't more encouraging:
7 out of 10 are worried about Beijing's military

00:04:58.250 --> 00:05:01.810
drive and believe that China's economic influence
is hurting them.

00:05:01.810 --> 00:05:05.690
In other words, it seems that both China and
India's population know that their neighbors

00:05:05.690 --> 00:05:07.960
are also their great rivals.

00:05:07.960 --> 00:05:15.730
In any case, curiously, it must be said that
despite all this rivalry Bollywood is becoming

00:05:15.730 --> 00:05:17.040
quite popular in China...

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:21.740
This summer, we saw how Dangal, an Indian
blockbuster, swept the Chinese box office

00:05:21.740 --> 00:05:27.350
and became one of the highest grossing films
in China of all time.

00:05:27.350 --> 00:05:31.810
Of course, well, the Beijing government does
not like this at all.

00:05:31.810 --> 00:05:35.930
Audio: “In terms of soft power, India has
done better than China [...] Although India’s

00:05:35.930 --> 00:05:40.680
economy is not as developed, they have put
a huge emphasis on promoting their culture”.

00:05:40.680 --> 00:05:46.160
Jiang Jingkui, director of the Southeast Asian
Research Institute at Peking University.

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:51.500
Anyway, it'd be great if all tensions occurred
in such a, let's say, peaceful field…

00:05:51.500 --> 00:06:01.330
But, unfortunately, that's not the case.

00:06:01.330 --> 00:06:04.500
DISPUTES IN THE HIMALAYAS

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:09.080
While everyone was looking at Pyongyang, and
the North Korean nuclear crisis occupied every

00:06:09.080 --> 00:06:14.900
front page, another political crisis was about
to explode.

00:06:14.900 --> 00:06:19.700
It happened in the Himalayas, more than 4000
meters above sea level, in one of the most

00:06:19.700 --> 00:06:23.530
remote places of Earth: the Doklam plateau.

00:06:23.530 --> 00:06:28.070
In this place, between June and August, one
of the most serious political crises between

00:06:28.070 --> 00:06:33.760
China and India in the last 55 years occurred:
when Chinese troops invaded northern India.

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:38.860
See, on June 8th, 2017, a squad of Chinese
border guards and a construction team entered

00:06:38.860 --> 00:06:43.389
a territory that is disputed between China
and the small, closed, kingdom of Bhutan.

00:06:43.389 --> 00:06:44.389
Bhutan?

00:06:44.389 --> 00:06:48.380
The country with the highest “Gross National
Happiness.”

00:06:48.380 --> 00:06:51.740
Yep, and that’ll certainly be something
we discuss one day.

00:06:51.740 --> 00:06:56.930
Well, the fact is that the Chinese units destroyed
several bunkers owned by the Bhutan Royal

00:06:56.930 --> 00:07:00.050
Army and began to build a road.

00:07:00.050 --> 00:07:06.449
However, as Bhutan's protection has been in
India's hands since the 40s, Indian troops

00:07:06.449 --> 00:07:10.070
arrived on June 16th and blocked the road's
construction.

00:07:10.070 --> 00:07:12.710
So far, a typical border conflict...

00:07:12.710 --> 00:07:23.410
However, tensions didn't dilute but increased…
and the discussions between Beijing and New

00:07:23.410 --> 00:07:24.910
Delhi became quite tense.

00:07:24.910 --> 00:07:25.910
“China and India are dangerously close to
military conflict in the Himalayas”.

00:07:25.910 --> 00:07:26.910
The Washington Post.

00:07:26.910 --> 00:07:31.720
The Chinese state media began to threaten
the Indian government with serious consequences…

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:38.090
So, at this point, you may be wondering,

00:07:38.090 --> 00:07:42.150
Why on earth was a land that is practically
frozen for most of the year given such importance?

00:07:42.150 --> 00:07:46.570
Well, on the one hand it seems that Xi Jinping's
government wanted to test India and "punish"

00:07:46.570 --> 00:07:48.480
them for... well, many things:

00:07:48.480 --> 00:07:52.510
For their relationship with the Dalai Lama
and Tibet, for their growing ties with Washington,

00:07:52.510 --> 00:07:55.320
for their relations with Pakistan, and so
on.

00:07:55.320 --> 00:07:59.020
And with regard to India, because China's
control in this area – with its military

00:07:59.020 --> 00:08:03.500
presence and new road - would put China within
a stone's throw of the so-called "Siliguri

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:07.930
Corridor", a narrow strip of land considered
strategic because it connects seven of the

00:08:07.930 --> 00:08:10.870
states of northeast India with the rest of
the country.

00:08:10.870 --> 00:08:14.620
You can see this well on the map.

00:08:14.620 --> 00:08:21.200
And above all, beyond tactical issues, for
another important reason.

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:27.650
The same reason why China wanted to test India...
you'll see what I'm talking about in a minute...

00:08:27.650 --> 00:08:31.889
The fact is that, finally on Monday, August
28th, after many strips and slacks, many threats

00:08:31.889 --> 00:08:36.380
and a lot of tension, both sides agreed to
withdraw their troops and return to the starting

00:08:36.380 --> 00:08:38.630
point of this entire political muddle.

00:08:38.630 --> 00:08:42.529
Of course, years ago both powers' rivalry
wasn't as obvious as it is now.

00:08:42.529 --> 00:08:47.190
And of course, let's not fool ourselves, the
Doklam plateau is... well… the least of

00:08:47.190 --> 00:08:48.190
it.

00:08:48.190 --> 00:08:51.660
And I'm not saying this just because of the
more than 3,000 km of border that have territorial

00:08:51.660 --> 00:08:53.589
disputes between China and India.

00:08:53.589 --> 00:08:54.589
There are...

00:08:54.589 --> 00:08:58.019
Many more reasons.

00:08:58.019 --> 00:09:04.139
A NATIONAL STRATEGY

00:09:04.139 --> 00:09:08.240
Given the possible emergence of India as a
superpower, the Chinese government has adopted

00:09:08.240 --> 00:09:10.700
a strategy: to surround it.

00:09:10.700 --> 00:09:13.439
Yeah, that’s exactly as it sounds what it
sounds like…

00:09:13.439 --> 00:09:18.730
In recent years China has tightened its ties
with Pakistan in exchange for $60 billion

00:09:18.730 --> 00:09:23.629
in infrastructure, especially to connect both
countries, including a strategic port in Gwadar

00:09:23.629 --> 00:09:28.389
that China will operate until at least the
year 2050…

00:09:28.389 --> 00:09:37.670
On the other hand, a Chinese government company
has taken control of Hambantota port in Sri

00:09:37.670 --> 00:09:42.100
Lanka, a country with which Beijing is also
strengthening political ties.

00:09:42.100 --> 00:09:45.790
Regarding Bangladesh, China has become its
most important arms supplier.

00:09:45.790 --> 00:09:48.130
Last year they sold them two submarines…

00:09:48.130 --> 00:09:53.050
And finally Nepal, which greatly improved
its relationship with China after a political

00:09:53.050 --> 00:09:55.589
conflict in 2015 with New Delhi.

00:09:55.589 --> 00:10:02.529
Now let's look at a map.

00:10:02.529 --> 00:10:04.050
See?

00:10:04.050 --> 00:10:06.620
India is surrounded.

00:10:06.620 --> 00:10:13.540
The Bhutan criss wasn't more than a move in
this chess game.

00:10:13.540 --> 00:10:18.680
A game in which China has the economic capacity,
and the money, to make friends easily.

00:10:18.680 --> 00:10:24.410
And of course, the fact that China's military
superiority over India is overwhelming is

00:10:24.410 --> 00:10:25.410
also very helpful.

00:10:25.410 --> 00:10:32.880
So a question that must arise is: after all
of this… what is India's bet, or rather,

00:10:32.880 --> 00:10:34.920
their response?

00:10:34.920 --> 00:10:38.730
Basically, three words: The United States.

00:10:38.730 --> 00:10:41.339
Yes, as you heard it.

00:10:41.339 --> 00:10:45.100
In recent years, relations between the United
States and India have become quite close.

00:10:45.100 --> 00:10:51.259
See, between 2009 and 2016 bilateral trade
doubled, and the sale of military equipment

00:10:51.259 --> 00:10:55.429
from the United States to India multiplied
by 50!

00:10:55.429 --> 00:11:02.269
In fact, everything indicates that India is
going to replace their old Mig 21 with a mega

00:11:02.269 --> 00:11:05.869
contract of newly manufactured F16s (200 of
them).

00:11:05.869 --> 00:11:10.529
And if this is confirmed, Lockheed Martin's
intention, the manufacturer, - with the Pentagon's

00:11:10.529 --> 00:11:14.700
approval, of course - is to transfer all of
this plane's worldwide production from Texas

00:11:14.700 --> 00:11:15.700
to India.

00:11:15.700 --> 00:11:21.029
An unbeatable way to strengthen alliances,
don't you think?

00:11:21.029 --> 00:11:26.179
Well, now we can better understand not only
China and India's tense relationship, but

00:11:26.179 --> 00:11:31.050
also, for example, the US's new hard strategy
towards Pakistan, which we discussed in our

00:11:31.050 --> 00:11:34.200
previous video about Afghanistan.

00:11:34.200 --> 00:11:43.790
And of course, all of this starts based on
a premise: India will emulate the economic

00:11:43.790 --> 00:11:47.230
success that China has achieved in recent
decades...

00:11:47.230 --> 00:11:51.540
Narendra Modi, the popular Indian Prime Minister,
of whom we already talked about, is leading

00:11:51.540 --> 00:11:52.610
many changes...

00:11:52.610 --> 00:11:55.160
But not as many as the country needs.

00:11:55.160 --> 00:11:57.640
But we can leave this for another day.

00:11:57.640 --> 00:11:58.759
Now, it's your turn.

00:11:58.759 --> 00:12:02.709
Do you think that China will succeed in beating
India?

